# The top-level package names the gpu-install phase asks apt for on a g5g.metal session, one per line as
# "<list> <name>", in three lists: driver (Ubuntu's archive, restricted), toolkit (NVIDIA's CUDA repository,
# ubuntu2404/sbsa) and build (Ubuntu's archive, main). Names only, never a version: both modes, plan and apply, ask
# for each name as name=version from the session's approved file, and the pin file the plan writes from that file
# holds the names apt is not asked for. @KREL@ is the running kernel's release (uname -r), the kernel ABI in the
# module package's name; a module package for any other ABI is refused. Neither a session nor its prep changes this
# file.
#
# The driver is Ubuntu's prebuilt, signed proprietary module for the running kernel (no DKMS build) with the 580
# server user space. No nvidia-modprobe: the udev rule and helper that nvidia-kernel-common-580-server installs make
# the device nodes, /dev/nvidia-uvm among them. No git and no curl: on an AMI that already has either at an older
# version, asking for it by version would be an upgrade, which the plan refuses. build-llama.sh refuses without git,
# and the vlm phase checks for curl by name.
driver linux-modules-nvidia-580-server-@KREL@
driver nvidia-kernel-common-580-server
driver libnvidia-compute-580-server
driver nvidia-utils-580-server
toolkit cuda-nvcc-13-2
toolkit cuda-cudart-dev-13-2
toolkit libcublas-dev-13-2
build cmake
